		{"id":"3a978a7822a9348d","type":"text","text":"[[The Age of Vasselhiem (Current).canvas]]\n[[Volstarian Dynasty]]\n#lore","x":-216,"y":-266,"width":456,"height":86},
		{"id":"88c1a4ff19f2318c","type":"text","text":"The Start of The War Between Nations\n10 years After the fall of Vecna, Askain wanted to claim all of his relics and artifacts for themselves, becoming hungry for power and wanting more information on dunamancy. Caesar and Volstar the king did not approve of the experiments and new intentions rising in their neighbouring nation and when they addressed those concerns all hell broke loose. Queen Asala of the country of Askain rejected the distrust and started a war. She had found out that Caesar had both the hand and eye of Vecna and wants them for herself as she needs to know the power those relics possess. (unbeknownst to all other people Kryn has been imprinted by Vecna and is doing his bidding, but nobody knows they all think she's just hungry for power). The war is at a forever stand still as the hero who once saved the world is burdened with purpose and cannot leave his post guardian the two evil artifacts for all of eternity.\nThe two parts of Vecna are in the open for anyone to take; they reside in a bag on his person as other than Vecna himself no person has ever been able to even lay a finger on Caesar. He is the most powerful mortal to ever exist. A true paladin.\n","x":-152,"y":-60,"width":785,"height":340}
	],
	"edges":[]
}